  "text_sanskrit": "उत्सीदेयुरिमे लोका न कुर्यां कर्म चेदहम् । सङ्करस्य च कर्ता स्यामुपहन्यामिमाः प्रजाः ॥ ३-२४ ॥",
  "itrans": "utsIdeyurime lokA na kuryA.n karma chedaham . sa~Nkarasya cha kartA syAmupahanyAmimAH prajAH .. 3-24 ..",
  "translation": "These worlds would perish, if I should not perform Karma; then I would be the author of confusion of castes, and I would be destroying these creatures. (24.) \nV. Parish: fall into misery and hell for omission of duty. Further, when duties are abandoned, the distinction between the castes would become effaced. Then the confusion of castes and the ruin of all beings should appear to proceed from Me. (24.) \nA. If the wise man also should perform duties with the same attachment as the ignorant, the action of both could not then differ.' This supposition is amended in the following.",
